                            <span class="notranslate" translate="no"><span style="color: #ff6b00;">Raah</span><span class="text-white">Sathi</span></span> strictly enforces zero-tolerance policy against service payment defaults. If a customer refuses to pay the final approved invoice upon completion of breakdown repair work, attempts to pay less than the total approved estimate, or flees the breakdown location without settling charges:
                        </p>
                        <ul class="text-light leading-relaxed mb-3" style="line-height: 1.8;">
                            <li><strong class="text-danger">Immediate Legal Action:</strong> <span class="notranslate" translate="no"><span style="color: #ff6b00;">Raah</span><span class="text-white">Sathi</span></span> legal cell will initiate formal criminal proceedings against the defaulting customer under Section 420 (Cheating &amp; Dishonesty) and Section 379/303 of the Indian Penal Code (IPC) / Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS).</li>
                            <li><strong class="text-danger">Police Complaint &amp; FIR Registration:</strong> Formal Police Complaints will be lodged at the nearest Police Station having jurisdiction over the breakdown location, providing recorded GPS logs, phone numbers, vehicle registration records, and live job audio/video proof.</li>
                            <li><strong class="text-danger">Account Blacklisting &amp; Recovery:</strong> The customer's mobile number, Aadhaar, vehicle registration, and device ID will be permanently blacklisted across all Indian RSA networks, and legal recovery notices will be dispatched for recovery of outstanding fees along with legal damages and penalties.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <div class="p-2.5 bg-dark bg-opacity-80 rounded text-warning small font-weight-bold d-flex align-items-center">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation me-2"></i> Notice: Honest service providers risk their lives on highways to rescue stranded drivers. Payment defaults will be prosecuted with maximum legal severity.
                        </div>
